<title>USA: Cablevision shrs jump on TCI deal.</title>
<headline>Cablevision shrs jump on TCI deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Cablevision Systems Corp jumped 5-7/16 to 40-1/16 in early Monday trade after it said it will buy 10 cable television systems in the New York area from Tele-Communications Inc for about $422.4 million in stock.</p>
<p>Cablevision, the sixth-largest cable operator in the United States, would get 820,000 new customers and give TCI, the nation's largest cable TV company, 12.2 million shares of Cablevision Class A stock.</p>
<p>TCI shares added 15/16 to 16.  </p>
<p>Cablevision was to hold a telephone conference call with analysts at 1100 EDT/1500 GMT.</p>
